      "ts": 1790201691.033372,
      "status": "done",
      "result": {
        "summary": "The T-1377 design is reproduced faithfully. Policy holds are unchanged: with no fallback tier, a complexity-9 fallback still holds with the same reason string. When no account has headroom or running Claude workers reach the cap, the task is requeued with hold_note claude_capacity and dispatched_at cleared. All four acceptance tests are present as unittest methods, and the file has import _harness and the daemon import. I did not run the gate; the packet reports it green on the first attempt, with no reds. One caveat: the worktree HEAD (0416c4e) equals the packet base, so I judged the change from the commit fc2ba04 diff, which is the cherry-pick source, rather than a live scoped diff.",
        "verdict": "approve",
        "comments": [
          {
            "path": "orchestrator/executor.py",
            "line": 558,
            "issue": "The requeue path reads the worker cap with pool.cfg.get('limits', {}).get('max_parallel_claude_workers', 4). The hardcoded default 4 could diverge from the pool.toml default if that key is ever absent. Non-blocking.",
            "severity": "low"
          }
        ],
        "packet_version": "72607f4af188",
